<header class="page-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">Privacy information</p><h1>How FurniCraft handles your information.</h1><p>This notice summarizes how FurniCraft uses account details, catalog activity, reservation requests, and room photos. Read the AI processing, retention, and deletion information below before using the service.</p></div></header>
<article class="panel vstack gap-3">
    <section><h2 class="h5">Registration verification records</h2><p>Registration verification records contain a hashed code, the requesting IP address, and timestamps. An hourly cleanup removes these records once a code has been used or expired for at least {{ (int) config('privacy.registration_verification_retention_hours', 24) }} hours. Records remain until the next successful cleanup. This removes verification metadata, not your account, and preserves codes that are still usable.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="h5">Room photos and AI consent</h2><p>Room photos are stored in private application storage and served only to the signed-in owner and authorized shop administrators. New uploads have EXIF and common image text metadata removed before storage. FurniCraft sends a room photo to {{ \App\Services\AiProvider::label() }} only when you explicitly select the optional AI consent checkbox for that photo. Without this consent, FurniCraft uses local planning guidance and does not send the photo to the selected AI provider. With consent, the photo may be sent to the selected AI provider for room analysis and placement checks; generated images are available only when a supported image provider is separately enabled. You can turn off future AI processing for an image or delete it; this cannot recall data already sent to the provider. Photos uploaded before this consent control was introduced are not retroactively treated as consented, and any prior provider processing cannot be undone by this setting.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="h5">Other account information</h2><p>We use your name and email to create and verify your account. A mobile number is required so the shop can contact you about reservation requests. Birthdate and gender are optional account details; if supplied, they are stored with your account, but are not used for account verification or furniture ranking. You can create an account and use furniture planning without providing either field.</p><p>FurniCraft also stores preferences, recommendation history, catalog interactions, chat questions and replies, and reservation requests to provide the service. Reservation, recommendation, and chat history is removed with your account through the self-service account deletion control. Operational privacy audit entries record consent, image transfer, deletion, and retention actions without storing the photo contents or your network address.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="h5">Retention and deletion</h2><p>Private room photos, generated previews, and their room records are deleted by a daily scheduled cleanup after {{ (int) config('privacy.room_image_retention_days', 90) }} days from upload (90 days by default). You can delete an image sooner from your room list. Deleting your account removes its room photos and room records immediately. Feedback reports are scheduled for deletion after 12 months. When an account is deleted, its linked feedback reports are anonymized, their subjects are removed, and messages are removed unless explicitly reviewed as free of personal data. An administrator may configure the room-photo retention period using <code>ROOM_IMAGE_RETENTION_DAYS</code>.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="h5">Local recommendations and AI chat</h2><p>FurniCraft ranks catalog products and creates recommendation summaries locally; generating recommendations does not send your preferences or ranked results to the selected AI provider. When the selected AI provider is configured and a chat question needs an AI-generated answer, FurniCraft sends the current question, selected furniture type, recommended products, and active catalog entries for that type to {{ \App\Services\AiProvider::label() }}. Product context can include names, categories, wood, finish, style, listed prices, dimensions, and recommendation reasons. Questions answered by local catalog rules, and replies handled locally when AI is not configured, are not sent. If an AI request fails after it has been sent, the question and context may already have reached the provider. Chat processing is separate from room-photo consent: leaving the photo AI checkbox off does not prevent a chat question from being sent. FurniCraft also stores chat questions and replies in your account history. Do not include sensitive personal information in chat messages.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="h5">External processing</h2><p>In the customer workflow, the selected AI provider is used for consented room-photo analysis, furnished-room preview generation when requested, and chatbot answers when local catalog rules do not answer the question. With your room-photo consent, room photos may be transmitted to {{ \App\Services\AiProvider::label() }} for analysis and generated previews. Chat questions that need an AI-generated answer may also be transmitted with the recommendation and active catalog context described above. The selected provider processes submitted content under the terms and data-handling conditions that apply to the account and service tier configured by the shop; provider-side logging and retention depend on those terms and settings and are separate from FurniCraft’s room-photo retention period. Review <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the selected provider’s current data-handling terms</a> before using AI features. Deleting content from FurniCraft cannot recall information already sent to the provider. Do not upload photos containing people, identity documents, or other sensitive information.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="h5">Questions or requests</h2><p>Use <a href="{{ auth()->check() && !auth()->user()->isAdmin() ? route('profile.edit') : route('home') }}">profile settings</a> to delete your account, or <a href="{{ route('feedback.create') }}">send a message to Lance Furniture Shop</a> about a data request.</p></section>
